  "details": "It was difficult to use because the action of holding the camera and pressing the function selection button overlapped.  So I thought about a different shape.  It would be a good idea for vr headset users and keyboard users to use different cameras.\n1. The camera has a handle.  \n2. When the camera is rotated, the position of the handle changes.  \n3. The camera has dials and push buttons, and functions can be selected.  (Timer, filter, etc.) \n4. It has a function to view taken photos and view with others.  \n5. There is a function to send the photos you were watching together.  (If you hold the camera together, it will be transmitted. Refer to the picture.) \n6. It will turn off if you shake it quickly or throw it.",
